    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Paul OConnor from Castle Estate Agents KW is proud to present this fine Victorian period detached family home and comes to the market in pristine condition, with a large walled garden set in the heart of Crumlin Village. Location could not be better beside shops, range of schools, public transport, sporting facilities and within easy access to the city centre and M50 network. \r\n\r\nInnismore House, originally known as Antwerp Cottage was constructed by a merchant who had business connections with the port of Antwerp. The date of construction would be circa 1860. The current owners have refurbished and upgraded the property and it is ready for immediate occupation. With all uPVC double glazing, gas fire central heating, ample off street parking together with an amazing private garden and planning permission in place for a further extension to include an extra downstairs reception/dining room and bedroom with bathroom upstairs. Planning reference 2529/18 Dublin City Council. The accommodation comprises an entrance hall, kitchen/breakfast room, dining room, living room, utility, downstairs w.c., 4 bedrooms {master en-suite}, family bathroom, with another separate w.c. \r\n\r\nViewing is strongly recommended.\r\n\r\nDirections\r\nTravelling on St Agnes Road with The Garda Station in the Village on your right hand side, about 50 mts on Innismore House will be on your right hand side - just after the entrance to Innismore estate. The entrance is just back off the main road with double silver painted entrance gates.\r\n\r\nNotice\r\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only.\r\n\r\nFeatures\r\nDetached Victorian period property\r\nSet in the heart of Crumlin Village\r\nPresented in walk-in condition\r\nGas fired central heating\r\nuPVC double glazing\r\nThe property has been further insulated, not reflected in the BER\r\nFabulous private garden, bordered by original garden walls\r\nAmple off street parking\r\nBeside shops, schools, public transport, restaurants, pubs and range of sporting facilities\r\nBER D1 No. 105163166\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\nAll information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to ourselves. While every care is taken in preparing particulars the firm do not hold themselves responsible for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get a professional opinion on any concern they may have."
      }
